Emerald 3DS changes to pret/pokeemerald 76463dac15cad36aca5e2b3f6366abf9e53f814f: Japanese Pokédex units and lines
Applies after 0077-japanese-placeholder-code.patch; apply with tools/bootstrap.py.

The Japanese Pokédex shows height and weight in meters and kilograms: the unit
templates (gText_EmptyHeight/gText_EmptyWeight, unused in the international game)
with the value over them (PrintDecimalNum), at that ROM's places. Its cry page reads
"<species>'s cry" and its size page "<species> and <player>'s size comparison", with
the pieces that ROM prints apart; its list names start a tile further right. The
Lotad and Seedot size records stay in centimeters, as the Japanese texts say, and the
decimal separator is that charset's period (0xB8). Other languages are unchanged.

diff --git a/src/field_specials.c b/src/field_specials.c
index b92efa1..de0a13e 100644
--- a/src/field_specials.c
+++ b/src/field_specials.c
@@ -191,7 +191,11 @@ static void DetermineCyclingRoadResults(u32 numFrames, u8 numBikeCollisions)
     if (numFrames < 3600)
     {
         ConvertIntToDecimalStringN(gStringVar2, numFrames / 60, STR_CONV_MODE_RIGHT_ALIGN, 2);
+#if GAME_LANGUAGE == LANGUAGE_JAPANESE
+        gStringVar2[2] = CHAR_COMMA; // The Japanese charset's period
+#else
         gStringVar2[2] = CHAR_DEC_SEPARATOR;
+#endif
         ConvertIntToDecimalStringN(&gStringVar2[3], ((numFrames % 60) * 100) / 60, STR_CONV_MODE_LEADING_ZEROS, 2);
         StringAppend(gStringVar2, gText_SpaceSeconds);
     }
